Description
===========
Send XEMBED messages with the _XEMBED atom rather than _NET_WM_NAME.

Xembed is index 1 of the xatom enum and NetWMName is index 1 of the netatom
enum. Four sendevent() calls in clientmessage() and one in maprequest() index
Xembed into netatom, so every XEMBED message the embedder sends carries
message_type _NET_WM_NAME instead of _XEMBED.

The system tray protocol has the embedder complete the XEMBED handshake by
sending XEMBED_EMBEDDED_NOTIFY once the icon is reparented. Mistyped, it never
arrives, and the icon stays half embedded: reparented and mapped, but never
told who its embedder is. updatesystrayiconstate() then sends
XEMBED_WINDOW_ACTIVATE and XEMBED_WINDOW_DEACTIVATE with the correct atom, so
the client receives activation changes for an embedding it was never notified
of.

Qt reports each mistyped message as

    qt.qpa.xcb: Unhandled client message: "_NET_WM_NAME"

which is how this surfaces in practice: keepassxc and telegram each log one
such line per send as their tray icon docks.

XEMBED_FOCUS_IN and XEMBED_MODALITY_ON are dropped rather than repaired. The
XEMBED specification has the embedder send FOCUS_IN only when it hands
keyboard focus to the embedded window, and a tray icon never takes keyboard
focus. Delivering it makes a Qt client call handleWindowActivated() on the
icon, treating a 23x23 embedded window as the application's active window.
MODALITY_ON states that the embedded window is shadowed by a modal dialog and
should stop responding, which is never true of a tray icon. Both are inert
while mistyped, so correcting the atom without removing them would introduce
behaviour the embedder never actually had.

XEMBED_WINDOW_ACTIVATE is kept. The bar that embeds the systray is always
active, which is what the message states.

